# [Asynchronous scheduling]($heading.id('scheduling-and-attention-workers'))

Availability can vary by model, backend, and release.

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--async-scheduling` | Off | Enable asynchronous scheduling on supported models. The initial beta covers Llama and Gemma 4 without speculative decoding. |


# [Sampling]($heading.id('sampling'))

`--top-k` acts as an upper bound on the sampled tokens.
`--temperature`, `--top-p` and `--min-p` can be set per-request using [Chat completion API]($link.page('llmd/reference/v1/chat/completions')
The model defaults generally come from model authors in the "model card".

| LLMD option | Fallback | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--top-k=<number>` | `model default` | Top-k sampling cutoff. |
| `--temperature=<number>` | `model default` | Sampling temperature controlling randomness. |
| `--top-p=<fraction>` | `model default` | Nucleus sampling probability threshold. |
| `--min-p=<fraction>` | `model default` | Minimum nucleus sampling probability threshold. |

# [System One]($heading.id('systemone'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--systemone-window=<number>` | Batch size / 4 | Number of questions from one `/v1/systemone` request in flight at once. |

# [Misc]($heading.id('misc'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--io-impl=<name>` | `zio` | Zig allows to dynamically change the I/O runtime.
We recommend [zio](https://github.com/lalinsky/zio), but `--io-impl=threaded` is also available using `std.Io.Threaded` |
